    "title": "pandas.api.types.is_dict_like — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.types.is_dict_like#\n\n- \npandas.api.types.is_dict_like(*obj* )[source]#\n- Check if the object is dict-like. An object is considered dict-like if it has the `__getitem__` ,`keys` , and`__contains__` attributes but is not a type itself.\n  - Parameters:\n    - **obj** object\n    - The object to check. This can be any Python object, and the function will determine whether it behaves like a dictionary.\n  - Returns:\n    - bool\n    - Whether obj has dict-like properties.\n See also \n  - `api.types.is_list_like`\n  - Check if the object is list-like.\n  - `api.types.is_file_like`\n  - Check if the object is a file-like.\n  - `api.types.is_named_tuple`\n  - Check if the object is a named tuple.\n Examples >>> from pandas.api.types import is_dict_like >>> is_dict_like({1: 2}) True >>> is_dict_like([1, 2, 3]) False >>> is_dict_like(dict) False >>> is_dict_like(dict()) True",
    "markdown_length": 878,
